sections.content:
Arrays:
const colors = ['red', 'green', 'blue'];
colors[0]        // 'red' (zero-indexed)
colors.length     // 3
colors.push('yellow')    // adds to the end
colors.pop()              // removes from the end

Objects:
const user = {
  name: 'Sam',
  age: 28,
  isActive: true
};
user.name          // 'Sam' (dot notation)
user['age']        // 28 (bracket notation, useful when the key is dynamic)
user.email = 'sam@example.com';   // adding a new property

Arrays of objects (an extremely common real-world pattern):
const users = [
  { name: 'Sam', age: 28 },
  { name: 'Riya', age: 34 }
];
users[0].name      // 'Sam'
users[1].age       // 34

